2. DEFINITIONS

2.1. “PulseSync Materials” means source code, scripts, configuration files, build tooling, templates, examples, documentation, assets, and other copyrightable materials that:
(a) are contained in a repository, package, SDK, template, release, or other distribution to which this License is attached;
(b) are provided by the Licensor or otherwise lawfully distributed by the Licensor under this License; and
(c) are not expressly identified as third-party materials governed by another license.

2.2. “Derived PulseSync Materials” means copyrightable portions of any modification, adaptation, translation, port, refactoring, transformation, derivative work, or other material that is based on PulseSync Materials and retains, reproduces, adapts, or incorporates protected expression from the PulseSync Materials.

2.3. A change of programming language, file structure, identifier names, formatting, module boundaries, build system, packaging, minification, bundling, transpilation, code generation, automated transformation, or AI-assisted transformation does not by itself prevent material from being Derived PulseSync Materials where protected expression from the PulseSync Materials remains incorporated or adapted.

2.4. “Developer Code” means original copyrightable code and materials independently created by You that do not reproduce, adapt, translate, or otherwise incorporate protected expression from the PulseSync Materials.

2.5. “PulseSync Addon” means software that:
(a) is designed to operate in, through, or in direct connection with PulseSync using an addon, plugin, extension, integration, SDK, API, or other mechanism intended for PulseSync;
(b) provides PulseSync-specific functionality directly to users of PulseSync or directly supports that functionality; and
(c) uses the PulseSync Materials or Derived PulseSync Materials only to the extent reasonably necessary for that PulseSync-specific functionality.

2.6. For purposes of this License, software is not considered a PulseSync Addon merely because it is technically compatible with PulseSync, can communicate with PulseSync, contains a nominal, incidental, dormant, or technically unnecessary PulseSync integration, imports PulseSync interfaces, or presents itself as a PulseSync addon while its relevant use of the PulseSync Materials serves an otherwise unrelated product.

2.7. “PulseSync Integration Layer” means the logically identifiable portion of multi-platform software whose specific function is to implement integration with PulseSync and which can reasonably be distinguished from the software’s shared core and integrations with other platforms.

2.8. “Development Product” means a reusable SDK, framework, library, addon template, starter template, starter kit, boilerplate, toolkit, code generator, scaffolding system, reusable development platform, or substantially similar product whose primary purpose is to facilitate development of other software rather than to provide end-user addon functionality.

2.9. “Authorized Purpose” means the development, testing, building, maintenance, operation, distribution, licensing, and commercial exploitation of PulseSync Addons in accordance with this License.

2.10. “You” means the individual or legal entity exercising rights granted by this License.

