6.2. In multi-platform software, PulseSync Materials and Derived PulseSync Materials may be included only within the PulseSync Integration Layer and only to the extent reasonably necessary to implement or support PulseSync-specific functionality.

6.3. PulseSync Materials and Derived PulseSync Materials may not be moved into, incorporated into, or used as the basis of a shared core, generic abstraction layer, common framework, common SDK, or integration layer for another platform.

6.4. Code that is independently created as Developer Code may remain in a shared core and may be licensed or reused by You without restriction under this License.

6.5. If PulseSync-specific code and shared code are technically bundled together, the absence of separate physical files does not remove the requirements of this Section. The relevant PulseSync-derived portions must remain logically attributable solely to PulseSync-specific functionality.

